    "content_excerpt": "The purpose of DNS is to spread scams Terence Eden shares some daunting statistics in support of his take that \"the Domain Name System's purpose seems to be a vector for criminals to run scams on people at a terrifyingly high rate\". On this Interisle report ( via Andrew Campling ), Terence says: It says 85 million new registrations of gTLDs were made in 2025. Of those 8.5 million were added to blocklists by May 2025. It reckons that a 10% abuse rate is the likely floor for these numbers and it's probably closer to 20%. One in five newly registered domains with a gTLD are scams. That's a bloody crisis. I had no idea. Apparently ICANN have been discussing this problem for years. Tags: dns , scams , terence-eden",
